{"title":"Career Roadmap · Analytical Chemist","role":"Analytical Chemist","summary":"An Analytical Chemist in the pharmaceutical sector applies chemical and instrumental analysis to identify, quantify, characterize, and evaluate pharmaceutical substances and products.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Pharm (Bachelor of Pharmacy)","Course":"Pharmaceutical Chemistry"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Analytical Chemist in the pharmaceutical sector applies chemical and instrumental analysis to identify, quantify, characterize, and evaluate pharmaceutical substances and products."},{"type":"h","text":"The role is important across:"},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmaceutical quality control"},{"type":"h","text":"Quality assurance"},{"type":"h","text":"Research & development"},{"type":"h","text":"Drug development"},{"type":"h","text":"Stability testing"},{"type":"h","text":"Raw-material testing"},{"type":"h","text":"Finished-product testing"},{"type":"h","text":"Method development and validation"},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmaceutical manufacturing"},{"type":"h","text":"Regulatory laboratories"},{"type":"p","text":"A pharmaceutical analytical chemist may work with active pharmaceutical ingredients (APIs), excipients, intermediates, formulations, impurities, degradation products, and packaging-related samples."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"10+2 / Intermediate"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"├── Physics"},{"type":"h","text":"├── Chemistry"},{"type":"h","text":"└── Biology / Mathematics"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"▼"},{"type":"h","text":"B.Pharm"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"▼"},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmaceutical Chemistry"},{"type":"h","text":"& Analytical Training"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"▼"},{"type":"h","text":"Laboratory Internship /"},{"type":"h","text":"Industry Exposure"},{"