"},{"type":"h","text":"ANALYTICAL CHEMIST"}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The strongest modern profile for an Analytical Chemist is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Pharm","Pharmaceutical Chemistry","HPLC/GC","Spectroscopy","Method Development & Validation","GMP/GLP","Statistics","Data Integrity","Digital Analytics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The key career advantage comes from combining strong chemistry fundamentals with hands-on instrumental analysis. A graduate who can confidently understand HPLC/GC data, perform scientifically sound analytical work, document results under quality systems, and use modern data tools will be well positioned for pharmaceutical QC, analytical R&D, contract testing, regulatory laboratories, and advanced analytical-science roles."}]}]}